== Policies
. Attendance and completion of readings before each class are expected. Laptops may be used for notes; please keep phones and other devices away during lecture and lab.
. Lab work is turned in before leaving the lab. A missed lab can be made up for full credit within one week with adequate notice; within two weeks it is worth half credit; after two weeks it will not be graded.
. Course materials, slides, and announcements are posted on [http://mycourses.stonybrook.edu Brightspace]. The last day to withdraw from a course is Fri, Apr 2.
. Audio or video recording of class sessions is not permitted, except for students with an approved accommodation from SASC.
. We follow the [https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/studentaffairs/sccs/conduct.php Code of Student Responsibility].
. We follow the University's [https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/academic_integrity/policies_procedures/index.php Academic Integrity Policy] (including on [https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/academic_integrity/generative-ai/index.php?accordion=content-d19e272 Generative AI and LLMs]); any use must be disclosed. Faculty are required to report suspected violations to the Academic Judiciary.
. If a disability may affect your coursework, contact the [mailto:sasc@stonybrook.edu Student Accessibility Support Center] (Stony Brook Union Suite 107, 631-632-6748) to arrange accommodations. All information is confidential. Students who may need help during an emergency evacuation are encouraged to discuss their needs with the instructor and SASC.
. Course materials posted online are for the exclusive use of students enrolled in this course and may not be redistributed, per the TEACH Act.
. Disruptive behavior that compromises the learning environment may be reported to the Office of University Community Standards.
